# Scenario 18: the blocked-with-no-parked-task, whole-run-question row and the blocked-with-parked-tasks row are mutually exclusive.
# A parked task present (whatever its decision_ref) must keep the whole-run-question clause from firing on its own -- dropping `and not parked` from that clause would let a parked task coexist with an unrelated whole-run question and still report a gap, which is not positive evidence for either of the two named rows.

